menu "CPU scheduler"

config SCHED_FAIR_REQUEST_US
    usize "Fair/EEVDF request length (microseconds)"
    range 100 100000
    default 2000
    help
      Default wall-clock request assigned to a Fair task on first
      enqueue. Virtual deadline uses this length. Default 2 000 (2 ms).

config SCHED_RR_SLICE_US
    usize "SCHED_RR time quantum (microseconds)"
    range 1000 1000000
    default 100000
    help
      How long a SCHED_RR task may run at its priority before rotating
      to the tail of that level. Default 100 000 (100 ms).

config SCHED_RT_PERIOD_US
    usize "RT bandwidth period (microseconds)"
    range 1000 10000000
    default 1000000
    help
      Length of the RT class throttle window. Paired with
      SCHED_RT_RUNTIME_US. Default 1 000 000 (1 s).

config SCHED_RT_RUNTIME_US
    usize "RT bandwidth runtime per period (microseconds)"
    range 0 10000000
    default 950000
    help
      How much CPU the whole RT class may consume in each
      SCHED_RT_PERIOD_US window before it is throttled so Fair can
      run. Values above the period are clamped to the period.
      Default 950 000 (0.95 s). Zero throttles RT immediately.

endmenu
